  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "s0001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Name",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "vfs_ceph_rgw — Use smb over object store provided by ceph librgw.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0003",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Synopsis",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "vfs objects = ceph_rgw"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0005",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "DESCRIPTION",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "This VFS module is part of the [[p0]] suite.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "link",
            "text": "samba(8)",
            "href": "https://www.samba.org/samba/docs/current/man-html/samba.8.html"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The [[p0]] VFS module exposes ceph-rgw hosted s3 bucket to users.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "vfs_ceph_rgw"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Ceph is a distributed network file system designed to provide excellent performance, reliability, and scalability. librgw is a shared library allowing applications to access an object store i.e. s3 bucket via a posix-like interface.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "This module can not be combined with other modules. librgw does not support renaming directories. Therefore the module internally ensures: [[p0]] for Samba to not use temporary names while creating directory and rename it to give name. librgw does not support random writes, therefore we do not implement async io write methods. Therefore, the module internally ensures: [[p1]] for samba to always use sync write method.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "link",
            "text": "vfs mkdir use tmp name = no",
            "href": "https://www.samba.org/samba/docs/current/man-html/smb.conf.5.html#VFSMKDIRUSETMPNAME"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "link",
            "text": "aio write size = 0",
            "href": "https://www.samba.org/samba/docs/current/man-html/smb.conf.5.html#AIOWRITESIZE"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0010",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "CONFIGURATION",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]] requires that the underlying share path is a s3 bucket name.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "vfs_ceph_rgw"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0012",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Since [[p0]] does not require a filesystem mount, the share [[p1]] is treated as root of the bucket and must be set to '/'. Any other path is ignored. In a ctdb cluster environment where ctdb manages Samba, [[p2]] must be configured to disable local share path checks, otherwise ctdb will not reach a healthy state.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "vfs_ceph_rgw"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "/"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "CTDB_SAMBA_SKIP_SHARE_CHECK=yes"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0013",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "GLOBAL OPTIONS",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0014",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The following options must be set in the global smb.conf section and won't take effect when set per share. librgw can only be initialised once per process, so these parameters are shared across all shares.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0015",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "ceph_rgw:id = name",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0016",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Client id portion of the Ceph client name used by librgw. (Required)",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0017",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Example: ceph_rgw:id = admin",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0018",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "ceph_rgw:config_file = path",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0019",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Allows one to define a ceph configuration to use. Default: /etc/ceph/ceph.conf",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0020",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Example: ceph_rgw:config_file = /etc/ceph/ceph.conf",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0021",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "ceph_rgw:keyring_file = path",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0022",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Allows one to define a ceph keyring file to use. (Required)",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0023",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Example: ceph_rgw:keyring_file = /etc/ceph/ceph.client.admin.keyring",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0024",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "ceph_rgw:debug = boolean",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0025",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Control debug logs for librgw. Default: off",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0026",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Example: ceph_rgw:debug = on",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0027",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "OPTIONS",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0028",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The following options can be set per share.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0029",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "ceph_rgw:user_id = name",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0030",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "User id of bucket owner. (Required)",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0031",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Example: ceph_rgw:user_id = samba",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0032",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "ceph_rgw:access_key = key",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0033",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Access key for bucket owner specified by user_id option. (Required)",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0034",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Example: ceph_rgw:access_key = samba-key",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0035",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "ceph_rgw:secret_access_key = key",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0036",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Secret access key for bucket owner specified by user_id option. (Required)",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0037",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Example: ceph_rgw:secret_access_key = samba-secret-key",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0038",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "ceph_rgw:bucket = bucket name",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0039",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Bucket name to be exported as share. (Required)",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0040",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Example: ceph_rgw:bucket = video4k",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0041",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Sample configuration",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0042",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "One needs access to working ceph cluster to configure samba to use this module. Following sample provides working samba configuration for an already existing ceph rgw object store and has pre-existing user, bucket and objects within bucket.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0043",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Install librgw-devel package",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0044",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "clone samba sources",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0045",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "configure samba as compile with option \"[[p0]]\" along with usual configuration options. Compile and install.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "--enable-cephrgw"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0046",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Edit smb.conf to include following share definition Note: path must be set to '/', any other path is ignored.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0047",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Start samba server",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0048",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "VERSION",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0049",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "This man page is part of version 4.25.0 of the Samba suite.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0050",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "AUTHOR",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0051",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The original Samba software and related utilities were created by Andrew Tridgell. Samba is now developed by the Samba Team as an Open Source project similar to the way the Linux kernel is developed.",
      "protected": []
    }
  ],
